\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Shine Thou upon us,Lord,
\par True Light of men,to-day;
\par And through the written word.
\par Thy very self display;
\par That so,from hearts which burn 
\par With gazing on thy face,
\par The little ones may learn
\par The wonders of thy grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Breathe Thou upon  us,Lord,
\par Thy spirit,s living flame,
\par That so with one accord
\par Our lips may tell thy name;
\par Give Thou the hearing ear,
\par Fix Thou the wandering thought,
\par That those we teach may hear
\par The great things thou hast wrought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Speak Thou for us,O lord,
\par In all we say of Thee;
\par According to thy word
\par Let all our teaching be;
\par That so thy lambs may know
\par Their own true sheperd's voice,
\par Where'er He leads them go,
\par And in His love rejoice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Live Thou within us,Lord;
\par Thy mind and will be ours;
\par Be Thou beloved adored,
\par And served,with all our powers;
\par That so our lives may teach
\par Thy children what Thou art,
\par And plead, by more than speech,
\par For Thee with every heart.
\par                        Amen. 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

